;; A `def` nested inside a top-level EXPRESSION must be rejected, and both the
;; compiled and the interpreted path must reject it the same way.
;;
;; It used to be accepted here: the `def` elaborated as a global (the type
;; checker was happy, and a later `main` could name it), but codegen emitted it
;; as a local of the enclosing statement, so the reference died in the emitted C
;; with `'answer_1326' undeclared`.  The only thing that ever caught it was the
;; synthesized-main fold relocating the statement into a function body -- which
;; happened only when the file declared no `main` of its own, so adding one made
;; the error vanish and the miscompile return.
;;
;; See docs/archive/turi-toplevel-expr-subforms-elaborate-in-global-scope.md
(if true (def answer 42) (def fallback 7))

(defn main [] : int answer)
